The architecture of the Production Monitoring System mobile application follows a client-server model where industrial machines generate production data that is 
processed by a backend server and stored in a database. The Flutter mobile application  communicates with the backend through RESTful APIs to fetch and display 
real-time production counts, graphs, machine status, alarms, reports, and notifications in a user-friendly interface. The flow of the application begins with user 
login authentication, after which the app periodically fetches live machine data and displays it on the dashboard. The system continuously monitors production 
thresholds and triggers local notifications when predefined conditions are met, while also allowing users to access reports, alarms, and work order modules 
before securely logging out of the application.
